WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:02.400
Let’s plot a two-bearing fix.

2
00:00:02.650 --> 00:00:04.500
Follow the diagram.

3
00:00:04.750 --> 00:00:07.375
At ten fifteen you take two bearings.

4
00:00:07.625 --> 00:00:10.275
A light bears three four zero true.

5
00:00:10.525 --> 00:00:13.275
A tower bears zero six five true.

6
00:00:13.525 --> 00:00:15.200
Start with the light.

7
00:00:15.450 --> 00:00:19.025
A bearing is the direction from you to the object.

8
00:00:19.275 --> 00:00:23.500
So from the light, which way do you draw the line back toward yourself?

9
00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:27.400
Along the reciprocal: one six zero.

10
00:00:27.650 --> 00:00:29.350
Now the tower.

11
00:00:29.600 --> 00:00:34.975
It bears zero six five, so from the tower you draw back along two four five.

12
00:00:35.225 --> 00:00:42.400
The two lines are eighty-five degrees apart, which is nearly ideal, and they cross at your ten fifteen fix.

13
00:00:42.650 --> 00:00:44.675
Circle it and label it.

14
00:00:44.925 --> 00:00:51.500
Then read its latitude and longitude from the scales, because that’s usually what the question asks for.
